BrainVault OpenCL experiment

The vendored argon2-gpu source is pinned to upstream commit
f5fce223d16769f202449c9b0837ad3533304acd (2018-08-17), by Ondrej
Mosnacek and contributors. The upstream repository carries an MIT LICENSE,
preserved as LICENSE-UPSTREAM-MIT. Several individual OpenCL host files also
carry GPL-2.0-or-later notices. This experiment therefore conservatively treats
the complete directory as GPL-2.0-or-later. It is distributed inside the npm
tarball as a separate optional executable together with complete corresponding
source and COPYING-GPL-2.0-or-later; it is never linked into the MIT CLI.

The compact permutation arrangement in data/kernels/argon2_kernel.cl was
adapted from hashcat 7.1.2 OpenCL/inc_hash_argon2.cl, authored by the
Netherlands Forensic Institute and marked MIT. The full MIT grant is the same
standard text preserved in LICENSE-UPSTREAM-MIT; the applicable author notice
is retained here.

BrainVault-specific integration and secure-erasure changes are Copyright (c)
2026 BrainVault contributors and distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later for this
directory only.
